# results and logs are regenerated by backtests
results/
*.log
log.txt
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
# secrets
# `.env` alone left `.env.local`, `.env.production` and every other suffix TRACKABLE, which
# was measured on 2026-09-14: `git check-ignore .env.local` said NOT ignored. The negation
# keeps the placeholder template, which carries no real value and is meant to be committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
live/secrets*.json
live/secrets.env
# Any credential file placed under live/, not just the two named above. ProjectX credentials
# belong in live/secrets.env; this covers a second file created by someone who did not read
# that far.
live/*.env
!live/*.env.example
# Per-venue, per-account human approvals written by mode.write_approval. Machine-local by
# design: a committed approval would let a fresh checkout carry authorisation for an account,
# which is the stale-artefact accident the approval mechanism exists to prevent.
live/approvals/
# machine-local paper-trading state and gates (never committed by automation)
live/log/
live/state/
live/HALT
live/APPROVED_PAPER.md
live/alerts.json
# editor / os noise
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
# OpenClaw temp
.fs-safe-*.tmp
.openclaw-smoke-test.txt
# intraday bar store (regenerated from IBKR)
data/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Obsidian vault and editor state — NEVER auto-commit these.
#
# `Quant Brain/` is a 255,897-file / 4.2 GB imported research vault containing a
# THIRD PARTY's project (github.com/DonovanWillis/QuantModel, authored on macOS
# under /Users/donov/) plus agent-orchestration payloads. It has been swept into
# this repository twice by unattended `git add -A`:
#   592e11a "dcfhtg"  2026-09-13 19:50  3,199 files / 1,674,621 insertions
#   bb4bbf8 "igkhghk" 2026-09-13 21:31  3,200 files / 1,675,180 insertions
# Both were unpushed and were reverted; recovery refs
# `accidental-vault-commit-592e11a` and `accidental-vault-commit-bb4bbf8` retain
# them. Neither contained a credential (verified: 0 secret-shaped additions).
#
# It also carries `Quant Brain/.codex/config.toml` with approval_policy="never"
# and sandbox_mode="danger-full-access", whose own header says it must not be
# committed, and `Quant Brain/.claude/helpers/auto-commit.sh`, which runs
# `git add -A` and pushes with AUTO_PUSH defaulting to true against THIS repo's
# public origin.
#
# Versioning the vault is a deliberate architectural decision, not an accident.
# If that decision is ever taken, commit explicitly with `git add -f` after
# removing the executable agent payloads. Until then it stays on disk, untracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Quant Brain/
.obsidian/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Regenerable lab cache. `research/lab_sessions.pkl` is 126 MB of pickled
# session frames written by `scripts/strategy_lab_run.py` and read back by
# `strategy_lab_report.py` and `strategy_lab_topstep.py`. It was committed once
# and GitHub's pre-receive hook rejected the push: 126 MB is above the hard
# 100 MB per-file limit, and the rejection blocks the WHOLE push, not just that
# commit. It was excised from the four unpushed commits on 2026-09-15.
#
# It is a cache, not a result: `research/lab_trades.parquet` is the durable
# artifact, and the pickle is rebuilt by re-running the lab. A fresh clone must
# do that before the two report scripts above will run.
#
# Pickle is also an unsafe deserialization format; a clone should regenerate it
# locally rather than receive one over the wire.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
research/lab_sessions.pkl
